      "statement": "sc-lint must provide a step form, such as a module step kind or a documented sc-lint lint subcommand, that runs a named sc_lint.* wheel helper module on the sc-lint kit's interpreter on every OS without a consumer-written per-OS interpreter path.",
      "quote": "The wheel-only helpers (`sc_lint.lint_cargo_deny`, `lint_cargo_shear`, `lint_manifests`, `lint_codespell`) have to be invoked as `.sc-lint/venv/bin/python -m ...` on every OS (`Scripts\\python.exe` on Windows). There is no step form that says \"run this module on the kit's interpreter\", so we carry a 3-line `_sc-lint-py` recipe with a per-OS interpreter path. A step kind like `{\"module\": \"sc_lint.lint_cargo_deny\"}` or a documented `sc-lint lint deny|shear|manifests|spell` subcommand would delete it.",
